<title>FRANCE: French Aug consumer spending up 3 pct, July down.</title>
<headline>French Aug consumer spending up 3 pct, July down.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in July and August in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>				   Aug   July    June    Aug 95  July 95</p>
<p> Total			  60.44  58.68   59.03    57.11    57.23</p>
<p> Total change		   3.0   -0.6     2.1	-	  -</p>
<p>(pct v pvs month)</p>
<p> Retail sector		39.13  38.92   39.07    38.18    38.11</p>
<p> Durables		     19.18  17.49   17.78    16.48    16.84</p>
<p> Textiles, leather	  11.42  11.66   11.72    11.43    11.49</p>
<p> Other			  29.84  29.54   29.53    29.19    28.90</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month on month unless stated)</p>
<p>				   Aug    July    June  Aug y/y</p>
<p> Total			    3.0   -0.6     2.1    5.8</p>
<p> Retail sector		  0.5   -0.4     3.6    2.5</p>
<p> Durables			 9.7   -1.6     1.7   16.4</p>
<p>    of which cars	    18.1   -2.4     1.9   32.2</p>
<p>    household equip	   4.0   -1.1     1.6    6.5</p>
<p> Textiles, leather	   -2.1   -0.6     8.9   -0.1</p>
<p> Other			    1.0    0.0    -0.1    2.2</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
